From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: nuno5645 <ntrjferreira@hotmail.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 01:11:43 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] South Park: The Fractured But Whole (01008F2005154000):
 profile, bare zlib Snowdrop shader caches

- shader_split: South Park stores its .mcache files as bare zlib streams (a 1 KB window, 64 KB blocks) without the
  20-byte record header of the Mario + Rabbids games; snowdrop_zlib finds and decodes them (4,614 stages).
- Profile for update 1.05 (v327680): Snowdrop's three-pool page allocator reserves 12 GB; the cuts keep its layout in
  4 GB (1.5 GB large, 512 MB of 512 KB pages, 2 GB of 64 KB pages), sized from the pools' use measured on the Mac.
- sdk_patches: SDK 8bb65519 takes the 64 MB node area and 32 MB alignment cuts.
- Docs: shaders.md, memory.md, the games table and the generated patch list.

Tested on the Mac: title, menus, New Game, cinematics, character creation and the prologue to the first interactive scene.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

Upstream-Status: forwarded seedds/nxnative#843
Reason: new game profile and the Snowdrop zlib shader cache it needs; goes when seedds/nxnative#843 merges
Issue: LNPANDY/NX2Apple#377

